@startuml
' Rendered with: plantuml -tsvg <file>.puml
' Fonts: Carlito is metric-compatible with Calibri, so it lays the diagram out
' at Calibri's advance widths even on hosts without Calibri installed. After
' rendering, the SVG font-family is widened to a fallback stack:
'   sed -i '' 's/font-family="Carlito"/font-family="Calibri, Carlito, Trebuchet MS, sans-serif"/g' <file>.svg
' PlantUML cannot emit that stack itself -- it single-quotes a comma-separated
' skinparam value, which SVG then reads as one bogus family name.
skinparam defaultFontName Carlito
skinparam TitleFontSize 24
title NVMe/Falcon — STORE (Write) Flow

' ─── TPU/GPU HOST (initiator side) ──────────────────────────────
box "<size:20><b>TPU/GPU Host (initiator)</b></size>" #F0F6FF
participant "Application\n(LMCache)" as APP
participant "NVMe-oF Initiator\n(nvme_rdma on Xeon)" as INIT
participant "Initiator IPU\n(Falcon / irdma verbs)" as IFAL
end box

' ─── KV Cache node (target side) ────────────────────────────────
box "<size:20><b>KV Cache node (target)</b></size>" #FFF8E8
participant "Target IPU\n(Falcon / irdma verbs)" as TFAL
participant "Target Xeon\n(nvmet-rdma + block layer)" as CPU
participant "Target DRAM" as TDDR
participant "NVMe SSD\n(namespace)" as SSD
end box

APP -> INIT: store(tokens, kv_tensor)
INIT -> INIT: Register TX MR containing payload;\nbuild SGL for target RDMA READ
INIT -> IFAL: SEND (NVMe-oF WRITE command capsule + SGL)
IFAL -> TFAL: Falcon reliable transport\n(wire)
TFAL -> CPU: Deliver NVMe-oF command\n(nvmet-rdma dispatch)

CPU -> CPU: Allocate request data buffers\n(nvmet_req_alloc_sgls)
CPU -> TFAL: Post RDMA READ\n(initiator TX MR → target DRAM)
TFAL -> IFAL: Falcon reliable transport\n(wire, RDMA READ pull)
IFAL -> INIT: Read from initiator TX MR
INIT --> IFAL: Payload
IFAL --> TFAL: Falcon reliable transport\n(wire)
TFAL --> TDDR: Payload lands in target DRAM
TFAL --> CPU: RDMA READ completion

CPU -> SSD: NVMe WRITE (FUA)
SSD --> TDDR: DMA payload from target DRAM
SSD --> CPU: Completion
CPU -> CPU: Free request data buffers\n(nvmet_req_free_sgls)

CPU -> TFAL: SEND (NVMe-oF completion capsule)
TFAL -> IFAL: Falcon reliable transport\n(wire, SEND)
IFAL --> INIT: Completion capsule received

INIT -> APP: NVMe-oF command complete

note over IFAL, TFAL
  Boundary: Falcon RDMA link (400-1600Gbps, MTU 4096).
  Both IPUs do fabric offload only — no NVMe logic.
end note

note over CPU, INIT
  Pull model: the initiator sends an NVMe-oF WRITE command capsule;
  the target (stock nvmet-rdma) posts an RDMA READ to pull the payload
  from the initiator's registered buffer, then commits to NVMe (FUA).
  No admission control — the pull is paced by ordinary flow control:
  negotiated SQ depth, per-QP RDMA-read credits (IRD/ORD), and
  landing-buffer availability. A busy SSD back-pressures only
  indirectly, by slowing buffer recycling.
end note
@enduml
